Custom DeepStream bounding-box parser for AIPV1EMI0001
=======================================================

One shared library, `libnvds_infercustomparser.so`, serves the three detector flavors.
Each flavor is an official COCO-pretrained model with 80 classes; the AI Processor
publishes three (`car`, `person`, `truck`, see `models/AIPV1EMI0001_Yolo_Detector/labels-rev3.txt`).
The parser therefore maps the COCO class to the AIP class and drops everything else:

    COCO person (0) -> person (1)      COCO car (2) -> car (0)      COCO truck (7) -> truck (2)

It converts the model outputs into `NvDsInferObjectDetectionInfo` for DeepStream's
`nvinferserver` (Triton backend). Boxes are in network-input pixels (640 x 640);
DeepStream rescales them to the frame.

| Function | Flavors | Model outputs |
|---|---|---|
| `NvDsInferParseCustomEfficientNMS` | `yolov7` | `num_dets`, `det_boxes`, `det_scores`, `det_classes` from the `EfficientNMS_TRT` plugin |
| `NvDsInferParseYoloEndToEnd` | `yolov10`, `yolo26` | `output0` with shape `[300, 6]`, rows of `x1 y1 x2 y2 score class`; NMS-free |

A function returns `false` and logs the reason when the output layers do not match what it
expects (number of layers, layer names or shape), so a flavor wired to the wrong parser
fails loudly instead of producing wrong boxes.

Build
-----

Built by `bin/build.sh` at the repository root, which runs `make` in this directory and copies
the library into `models/AIPV1EMI0001_Yolo_Detector/`:

    bin/build.sh <flavor>

It needs the DeepStream headers and the CUDA toolkit present in the station's `ms8_jupyter`
container (`CUDA_VER` is passed by `bin/build.sh`).

Usage
-----

Each flavor's `configs/config_infer_primary_detector_<flavor>.txt` selects its function, for example:

    postprocess {
      detection {
        custom_parse_bbox_func: "NvDsInferParseYoloEndToEnd"
      }
    }
    custom_lib {
      path: "../models/AIPV1EMI0001_Yolo_Detector/libnvds_infercustomparser.so"
    }

Test
----

`tests/parser_stub/parser_harness.cpp` compiles the parser against a minimal stub of the DeepStream
header and checks both functions, including malformed outputs. It runs from
`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` and is skipped when no C++ compiler is available.
